  "question": {
    "text": "The empirical formula for a compound with a cubic close packed arrangement of anions and with cations occupying all the octahedral sites in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (Integer answer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math><br />Effective number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> atoms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> (in CCP)<br />Effective number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> atoms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> (all O.V.)<br />So formula of the compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>AB</mi></math><br />So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
